WEBVTT

00:05.797 --> 00:07.924
[Oz] So, who's got the power
in this city?

00:07.924 --> 00:10.051
- [sirens in distance]
- [dramatic music playing]

00:10.051 --> 00:11.302
[Oz] The Falcones?

00:12.637 --> 00:13.972
Sofia's the last of them.

00:14.097 --> 00:16.391
She don't even like
her fucking name. [chuckles]

00:16.391 --> 00:17.809
Maronis?

00:17.934 --> 00:19.894
Sure, Sal's out of Blackgate,

00:19.894 --> 00:21.479
but his family's
still fucking ash.

00:22.272 --> 00:24.649
So, who's got the power, huh?

00:25.608 --> 00:27.152
That's what
the streets are asking.

00:28.028 --> 00:29.070
But down here,

00:29.779 --> 00:30.822
we know.

00:31.322 --> 00:33.825
- [motorcycle engine revving]
- [dramatic music playing]

00:43.835 --> 00:45.378
[Oz] We started
with two buckets,

00:45.503 --> 00:47.172
two fuckin' buckets. That's it.

00:48.173 --> 00:51.426
And now, it's grown
into an underground empire.

00:51.426 --> 00:53.845
Cookin' and sellin' Bliss
under our label.

00:54.804 --> 00:57.349
You know how many boroughs
there are in Gotham?

00:58.391 --> 01:00.643
Each one run
by a different crew.

01:00.643 --> 01:03.063
All of them looking
for a way to get theirs.

01:04.689 --> 01:07.776
The more drugs we smuggle,
the more cash we bring in.

01:07.776 --> 01:08.943
That's food on the table

01:08.943 --> 01:10.570
and clothes
on your backs, fellas.

01:13.615 --> 01:15.492
And look, this ain't
the game you're used to.

01:15.492 --> 01:18.203
I get it.
You won't see any trouble.

01:18.328 --> 01:20.538
As long as your mouths
stay shut, you understand?

01:20.997 --> 01:23.625
Silence is golden,
loose lips, and all that shit.

01:23.625 --> 01:25.710
Remember, if somebody asks you
where you got this cash...

01:25.835 --> 01:27.420
- I say construction.
- Construction.

01:27.420 --> 01:28.755
We're all in construction.

01:29.214 --> 01:30.465
He has returned.

01:30.465 --> 01:32.092
Well, what did Donny Boy say?

01:32.092 --> 01:33.176
He's stoked.

01:33.176 --> 01:34.636
Sullivans moving our product
or what?

01:34.636 --> 01:36.763
Said they could sell Bliss
as fast as we can make it.

01:36.763 --> 01:38.723
Fuckin' right, they can.
Show me what you got.

01:39.432 --> 01:41.601
Kid, kid, not bad.

01:41.726 --> 01:43.269
Make a businessman
out of you yet.

01:45.188 --> 01:46.773
If we can get
a couple more gangs onboard,

01:46.898 --> 01:47.982
we're fuckin' set.

01:48.525 --> 01:49.818
Check this out.

01:49.818 --> 01:52.654
We finally got the line cleared
to Burnley, right?

01:52.654 --> 01:54.948
Means we can supply
the Massive now, too.

01:55.573 --> 01:57.617
- Oh, that's awesome.
- Look. Boom, boom, boom.

01:57.742 --> 01:58.785
But there's a lot bad blood

01:58.910 --> 02:00.328
between them
and the Odessa Mob, right?

02:00.328 --> 02:01.871
All these gangs
fucking hate each other.

02:01.871 --> 02:03.623
So we gotta make sure
that nobody advertises

02:03.748 --> 02:05.625
that we're, uh... you know,
we're dating around.

02:05.750 --> 02:06.668
- [chuckles]
- All right?

02:06.668 --> 02:08.545
Fuck this.

02:08.545 --> 02:10.005
Jesus Christ!

02:10.005 --> 02:11.464
Anyway, Bruno's got Odessa.

02:11.464 --> 02:13.591
I got Nick taking care
of the LoBoys.

02:13.717 --> 02:15.176
I even got Link.
He's hitting me up,

02:15.176 --> 02:16.511
saying Zhao
might wanna play ball

02:16.511 --> 02:18.263
now he sees all the money
we got coming in.

02:18.388 --> 02:20.640
- Oh, really?
- Yeah, greedy fuck.

02:21.141 --> 02:22.809
But the Triads,
they got the connects

02:22.934 --> 02:24.477
to take our operation
international.

02:24.477 --> 02:26.813
It's a whole different sport.
That's where all the money's at.

02:29.232 --> 02:31.651
Hey, Zeke. Zeke!

02:32.777 --> 02:34.029
Where are we at with the power?

02:34.029 --> 02:35.613
Gennies ain't gonna
hold us much longer.

02:35.739 --> 02:36.781
I'm working on it, boss.

02:36.906 --> 02:38.366
But City Hall's rationing
electricity,

02:38.366 --> 02:39.951
sending it all
to the rich neighborhoods.

02:40.076 --> 02:41.536
Of course they are,
fucking pricks!

02:41.536 --> 02:42.954
All right, just keep trying.

02:43.997 --> 02:45.040
Good, fellas?

02:45.623 --> 02:47.375
Oz, uh...

02:47.375 --> 02:49.294
- When I made that drop...
- Yeah?

02:49.753 --> 02:51.671
...uh, someone had eyes on
the Sullivans.

02:52.255 --> 02:54.507
- Whaddya mean?
- Think it was probably one of...

02:54.632 --> 02:57.552
S-Sal or Sofia's guys.

02:57.552 --> 02:59.262
- Yeah?
- He tried to follow me.

02:59.262 --> 03:00.305
He see you go underground?

03:00.805 --> 03:01.848
No. No.

03:01.973 --> 03:03.683
- You sure?
- Positive.

03:03.808 --> 03:05.435
All right. As long
as we stay sharp

03:05.435 --> 03:06.895
and duck 'em in the tunnels,

03:06.895 --> 03:08.605
these Maroni-Gigante-
Whatever-the-Fucks

03:08.605 --> 03:09.898
can sniff around all they want.

03:09.898 --> 03:11.649
They're so busy
with their noses up,

03:12.275 --> 03:14.027
they'll never think
to look down.

03:14.152 --> 03:15.278
But you and me...

03:15.278 --> 03:17.906
Look around.
Look at what we got, kid.

03:18.448 --> 03:21.576
The good people of Crown Point
hard at work, right?

03:21.576 --> 03:22.952
Protecting us.

03:22.952 --> 03:25.038
Keeping this whole fucking thing
quiet.

03:25.663 --> 03:27.082
We got their loyalty.

03:27.832 --> 03:29.042
And we got their love.

03:29.042 --> 03:30.168
You know why?

03:31.795 --> 03:32.712
'Cause we pay 'em.

03:32.837 --> 03:33.713
Hmm.

03:34.297 --> 03:36.007
You know how meaningful
that is, Vic?

03:37.300 --> 03:38.468
To be the guy
in the neighborhood

03:38.468 --> 03:39.552
who takes care of people?

03:41.846 --> 03:44.099
They're gonna tell stories
about us one day, kid.

03:45.684 --> 03:46.935
You think?

03:46.935 --> 03:48.228
I fuckin' know it.

03:48.353 --> 03:49.521
Victor Aguilar.

03:51.523 --> 03:52.691
Oswald Cobb.

03:53.900 --> 03:54.776
Yeah.

03:55.485 --> 03:57.112
Our names
are gonna live forever.

03:57.112 --> 03:59.197
["Take Me" by Karen Dalton
playing]

03:59.989 --> 04:01.700
♪ Take me ♪

04:03.493 --> 04:06.454
♪ To your darkest room ♪

04:08.081 --> 04:10.834
♪ Close every window... ♪

04:11.376 --> 04:15.672
[breathing heavily]

04:15.672 --> 04:17.132
[dress zips]

04:19.551 --> 04:20.760
You're doing it again.

04:22.053 --> 04:25.140
♪ The very first moment, I... ♪

04:25.140 --> 04:26.433
You're scrutinizing.

04:27.851 --> 04:29.102
I'm admiring you.

04:30.562 --> 04:31.521
Are you hurt?

04:31.521 --> 04:34.399
♪ I'd be in darkness... ♪

04:34.524 --> 04:37.569
I deserve it.
[breathing heavily]

04:38.111 --> 04:39.237
[sighs]

04:43.199 --> 04:44.284
♪ Take me... ♪

04:45.744 --> 04:47.370
Bored with me already?

04:47.370 --> 04:48.496
I have work.

04:53.752 --> 04:55.086
When you find Oz,

04:56.546 --> 04:58.965
feel free to take advantage
of my expertise.

05:01.509 --> 05:02.844
Dom will see you out.

05:03.845 --> 05:05.096
[song ends abruptly]

05:09.893 --> 05:12.520
["Beeveh" by Giti Pashaei
playing]

05:13.855 --> 05:14.731
[liquid bubbling]

05:16.775 --> 05:17.734
[liquid splashes]

05:23.406 --> 05:25.867
You know, fugitives really
shouldn't leave their rooms.

05:30.830 --> 05:31.998
[Salvatore sighs]

05:32.123 --> 05:36.252
[crunching, sighs]

05:36.252 --> 05:39.547
[Salvatore chopping]

05:42.342 --> 05:43.301
[exhales softly]

05:44.135 --> 05:45.553
I can't believe you opened that.

05:45.553 --> 05:47.972
What? It was just
gathering dust.

05:48.765 --> 05:49.974
Just like your father.

05:50.767 --> 05:51.643
[Sofia chuckles]

05:52.268 --> 05:53.478
- [glass clinks]
- [wine pouring]

06:05.156 --> 06:06.366
[Salvatore sighs]

06:08.284 --> 06:09.494
Do you want this chopped?

06:10.203 --> 06:11.246
Sure.

06:11.246 --> 06:13.665
[chopping]

06:16.793 --> 06:18.753
Leo spotted Oz's driver
delivering product

06:18.753 --> 06:20.088
in Sullivan territory.

06:20.547 --> 06:21.423
And lost him.

06:22.048 --> 06:23.717
Said he disappeared.

06:23.842 --> 06:25.343
Just like the others.

06:25.468 --> 06:27.345
Oz is a fucking weed.

06:28.179 --> 06:30.265
He likes the spotlight too much
to stay hidden.

06:31.516 --> 06:32.726
Don't use those.

06:38.857 --> 06:39.733
These are better.

06:42.569 --> 06:44.029
I wouldn't have pegged you
as a cook.

06:44.154 --> 06:45.613
Well...

06:45.613 --> 06:48.199
Nadia showed me
her family recipes.

06:50.326 --> 06:51.953
So I could pass 'em down.

06:54.164 --> 06:55.206
This is...

06:56.166 --> 06:57.834
khoresh bademjan.

06:57.834 --> 07:00.128
Eggplant, tomatoes,
a little meat.

07:01.713 --> 07:02.714
Taj...

07:03.882 --> 07:05.216
liked yogurt on his.

07:08.386 --> 07:11.181
[Salvatore sighs deeply]

07:11.181 --> 07:12.557
[whispers indistinctly]

07:13.641 --> 07:14.726
Mmm.

07:15.435 --> 07:16.603
Mangia.

07:17.604 --> 07:20.231
[spoon clinking]

07:22.984 --> 07:24.069
[Sofia] Mmm.

07:36.122 --> 07:37.165
Taj was right.

07:38.667 --> 07:40.418
It is very good with the yogurt.

07:41.586 --> 07:42.671
[Salvatore chuckles]

07:42.671 --> 07:44.589
[inhales sharply]
"Taj was right."

07:48.385 --> 07:49.594
[somber music playing]

07:49.719 --> 07:51.262
[inhales deeply, slams spoon]

07:56.476 --> 07:57.519
Okay.

08:00.063 --> 08:01.272
So the weed...

08:03.400 --> 08:05.110
The weed is sneaking around
the city

08:05.985 --> 08:07.112
without protection.

08:08.488 --> 08:10.323
He's supplying the street
with your drug.

08:10.949 --> 08:12.200
And no one's talking.

08:13.952 --> 08:15.787
If he gets more local gangs
on his side--

08:15.912 --> 08:16.955
No.

08:17.664 --> 08:20.041
He needs the Triads
to make waves,

08:20.041 --> 08:21.793
and they made a deal with me,
not Oz.

08:21.918 --> 08:24.129
Sofia, people buy
from whoever's selling.

08:24.254 --> 08:26.172
Oz got that tip from Carmine.

08:30.802 --> 08:31.803
Yeah.

08:32.721 --> 08:33.972
Stings, don't it?

08:36.975 --> 08:39.978
Well, then I think that we just
have to make it very clear

08:41.104 --> 08:43.690
that playing with Oz
comes at a cost.

08:46.484 --> 08:48.862
- [jackhammers running]
- [sirens in distance]

08:51.990 --> 08:53.033
[Oz sighs]

08:58.997 --> 09:02.250
["The Glow-Worm"
by The Mills Brothers playing]

09:05.670 --> 09:06.546
[electricity crackles]

09:06.671 --> 09:07.672
[song ends abruptly]

09:08.298 --> 09:09.257
The fuck?

09:09.257 --> 09:10.717
[clicking]

09:16.890 --> 09:17.932
[rattling]

09:20.810 --> 09:22.937
[generator engine sputters]

09:22.937 --> 09:24.147
[Francis] Oswald?

09:24.147 --> 09:26.608
[generator sputters]

09:26.608 --> 09:27.901
[Francis] Oswald?

09:29.069 --> 09:30.653
The fuckin' heat's off.

09:30.653 --> 09:32.238
Yeah, Oz, power's out.

09:32.238 --> 09:33.281
All right, I heard ya.

09:33.281 --> 09:34.491
My hands are freezing.

09:34.491 --> 09:36.159
Still smells fucking great,
though, huh?

09:36.159 --> 09:38.370
- Take a look.
- [Oz] Cooked enough.

09:41.664 --> 09:43.708
Kinda reminds me
of Paulie's Diner.

09:43.833 --> 09:44.668
Don't it, Ma?

09:46.336 --> 09:47.879
If you're gonna keep me
cooped up in here

09:48.004 --> 09:49.339
like a goddamned POW,

09:49.339 --> 09:52.217
the least you could do
is let me listen to my music.

09:52.342 --> 09:54.636
Thank you, sweetheart.
You're a good boy.

09:54.636 --> 09:56.054
Ma.

09:56.846 --> 09:59.516
Yeah, well, Ma, we ain't gonna
be here much longer,

09:59.516 --> 10:01.559
not with all the cash
we got coming in.

10:01.559 --> 10:02.936
Ain't that right, Vic?

10:03.520 --> 10:05.105
- Vic!
- Oh, oh, yeah, yeah.

10:05.105 --> 10:06.731
Yeah. Big money.
Yeah. Good stuff.

10:07.482 --> 10:08.942
Ma, eat something. Come on.

10:08.942 --> 10:11.361
You gotta keep your strength up.
A little bit of food.

10:11.361 --> 10:12.821
[chuckles]

10:12.821 --> 10:14.656
Paulie's Diner, huh?

10:15.281 --> 10:18.243
Ugh. Sticky, plastic menus.

10:18.743 --> 10:20.453
- Yeah.
- [Francis] Yeah.

10:20.453 --> 10:22.789
[laughs] You remember. Yeah.

10:22.914 --> 10:25.667
They... They... They...

10:26.918 --> 10:28.503
- Uh...
- [Oz] She ain't lyin'.

10:28.503 --> 10:29.879
- [Francis] They...
- Listen.

10:29.879 --> 10:32.132
The locals you brought in,
they're solid, tough.

10:32.257 --> 10:34.134
Anyone new,
they gotta have little hands.

10:34.592 --> 10:35.760
Did you say "little hands"?

10:35.885 --> 10:38.096
No, I'm fuckin' serious.
I mean, we can't have

10:38.221 --> 10:40.223
all these fat fingers
packing up our product.

10:40.223 --> 10:43.268
- Takes them twice as long.
- Okay. I got you.

10:43.601 --> 10:46.271
For Christ's sake, when are you
gonna do something, huh?

10:46.980 --> 10:48.606
Like it or not,
they're your boys.

10:48.732 --> 10:51.526
- They're fuckin' freezin'.
- Ma, what are you talkin' about?

10:51.526 --> 10:52.902
No! No!

10:52.902 --> 10:55.238
If you can't get the heat
back on, I'll go to Rex.

10:55.238 --> 10:57.490
- He'll get it done.
- Ma, hey. You're confused.

10:57.490 --> 10:58.992
Hey, you're just confused.

10:58.992 --> 11:01.453
I ain't Dad. All right?
Just snap out of it. Come on.

11:01.453 --> 11:03.747
Hey, you don't have to worry
about that, Francis, okay?

11:03.747 --> 11:05.707
- 'Cause Jack...
- Jack?

11:05.707 --> 11:07.208
Jack went to pay the bill
downtown.

11:07.208 --> 11:09.336
- What are you doing?
- So that's all settled, okay?

11:09.336 --> 11:11.087
Electricity, that's gonna be
back on soon.

11:11.087 --> 11:12.797
Jack's downtown?
This whole time...

11:12.922 --> 11:14.883
- He's gonna get it figured out.
- ...Jack's downtown.

11:14.883 --> 11:16.593
Stop it. You're making it worse.

11:16.593 --> 11:18.386
- I'm sorry. I thought--
- Hey, no, no.

11:18.970 --> 11:20.722
You don't talk about my brother.

11:20.722 --> 11:22.557
You ain't got no right,
you understand?

11:25.977 --> 11:27.979
Okay. Ma. Ma, look at me.

11:28.104 --> 11:29.981
Hey, Ma, look at me.

11:30.106 --> 11:31.191
I'm Oswald.

11:31.316 --> 11:33.068
I ain't Dad, all right?

11:33.068 --> 11:35.153
Jack and Rex, none of them
are here no more.

11:36.029 --> 11:37.572
[phone ringing]

11:37.572 --> 11:38.823
[Oz] It's just you and me.

11:39.616 --> 11:41.576
- You got it?
- Yes.

11:41.576 --> 11:42.535
- [Oz] Link?
- [Link] Oz.

11:42.994 --> 11:45.080
What's good? Mr. Zhao ready
to put in or what?

11:45.080 --> 11:47.040
Answer the phone, why don't ya?

11:47.332 --> 11:48.333
[Oz] Link.

11:49.000 --> 11:50.585
[plate clatters]

11:51.670 --> 11:53.171
- [Francis] Oswald.
- Huh?

11:53.296 --> 11:54.172
I know what's going on.

11:54.464 --> 11:55.632
What the hell
you talking about?

11:55.632 --> 11:57.133
I'll take care of my music.

11:57.133 --> 11:58.677
Hey, pull up the news.

11:59.886 --> 12:00.845
Link, come on.

12:00.970 --> 12:02.305
You clean this shit up.

12:02.305 --> 12:04.933
I'll take care of myself. Watch.

12:04.933 --> 12:06.685
Nah, it can't be that bad.

12:08.353 --> 12:09.562
Fuck!

12:09.562 --> 12:10.689
Triads are out.

12:11.398 --> 12:12.524
Shit!

12:13.650 --> 12:15.485
[reporter] Three bodies
have been found hanging.

12:15.485 --> 12:16.903
[Victor]
That's Sullivan territory.

12:17.028 --> 12:18.488
[reporter] All appear
to be young men,

12:18.488 --> 12:20.115
each of them
with a severed finger.

12:20.115 --> 12:21.825
[Oz] The hanging and the pinky?

12:21.825 --> 12:23.827
Jesus, Sofia,
pick a fucking lane.

12:23.827 --> 12:26.162
Why these guys?
They're just the corner boys.

12:26.162 --> 12:27.706
It's a warning shot.

12:27.831 --> 12:29.457
Fuckin' Mork and Mindy
are flexing.

12:29.457 --> 12:31.376
It means anyone caught
with our product gets it.

12:31.376 --> 12:33.336
[reporter] ...string of murders
comes on the heels

12:33.336 --> 12:34.546
of the escape of Salvatore...

12:34.671 --> 12:35.922
None of those
lightweight assholes

12:36.047 --> 12:37.841
have the balls
or the muscle to fight back.

12:37.966 --> 12:40.051
[reporter] ...gas leak that left
many prominent members

12:40.176 --> 12:41.678
of the Falcone Family dead.

12:41.678 --> 12:44.389
This close to a deal
with the Triads.

12:47.267 --> 12:49.811
Now, I couldn't give Bliss away
if I fucking tried.

12:57.193 --> 12:58.278
Unless...

13:03.575 --> 13:04.868
What if I did?

13:06.411 --> 13:07.579
What if you what?

13:07.704 --> 13:09.247
What if I gave it the fuck away?

13:14.711 --> 13:16.254
[Oz] Hey, everybody, listen up.

13:16.755 --> 13:18.465
I don't want anybody
to be shy tonight.

13:18.465 --> 13:20.925
You drop the product
in any diner, any bar,

13:21.051 --> 13:22.927
any fuckin' restaurant,
gas station.

13:23.053 --> 13:24.387
I don't give a fuck.

13:24.387 --> 13:27.432
Anybody who wants it gets it.
You understand? Anybody.

13:27.557 --> 13:29.601
- [man] Yeah, got it.
- These gangs, they've gotta know

13:29.726 --> 13:31.728
that Bliss is in their hood

13:31.728 --> 13:33.688
whether they fuckin' like it
or not.

13:34.147 --> 13:37.901
Look, Sal, Sofia know my crew.
They ain't lookin' for you guys.

13:37.901 --> 13:39.277
But we don't take
anyone's money?

13:39.402 --> 13:40.862
Nah. That's the beauty of it,
Richie.

13:40.862 --> 13:42.822
It ain't about the money,
not tonight, anyway.

13:42.947 --> 13:44.366
We're creating demand.

13:44.366 --> 13:46.951
Gonna give every motherfucker
in this city a free taste.

13:47.077 --> 13:49.204
All right, no more
standing around! Come on!

13:49.204 --> 13:50.747
Let's go! Let's go!

13:50.747 --> 13:52.624
Gotta get this shit
on the streets.

13:52.749 --> 13:55.794
[motorcycle engines revving]

14:01.257 --> 14:02.592
Hey, yo, Victor.

14:02.592 --> 14:04.302
What's good, man?
Where you been?

14:05.136 --> 14:06.137
Hey, Squid, what's up?

14:06.262 --> 14:08.223
Figured you had either bounced
or died.

14:08.223 --> 14:09.974
What are you doing
back in the Point?

14:10.642 --> 14:12.018
Run out of gas or something?

14:12.143 --> 14:13.728
Yeah, yeah. Uh-huh.

14:14.187 --> 14:15.814
Damn! You a sneakerhead now,
Victor?

14:16.272 --> 14:18.149
Nah, nah. These are, uh...

14:18.274 --> 14:19.484
These are just B-grade.

14:19.609 --> 14:21.903
B-grade? Come on, man.
Don't do me like that.

14:21.903 --> 14:23.613
We go back, right?

14:23.613 --> 14:25.573
Come on. You think
I can't see that shit?

14:28.952 --> 14:30.995
Yo, where you gettin'
your money from, Victor?

14:31.705 --> 14:33.957
'Cause other people in the Point
are flush with cash too,

14:33.957 --> 14:35.667
but not from Drops.
That shit dried up.

14:35.792 --> 14:36.751
So what is it?

14:37.627 --> 14:39.671
Squid, I'm not a part
of any drug--

14:40.588 --> 14:42.173
What? Huh?

14:44.217 --> 14:46.553
Squid, I-I don't know
what you're talking about, man.

14:46.553 --> 14:49.055
Oh, come on, man.
Don't fuckin' bullshit me, man.

14:49.180 --> 14:50.849
What about that old lady
I saw you with

14:50.974 --> 14:52.600
up by Calvin's the other night?

14:52.600 --> 14:55.311
What's good with her?
I haven't seen her in a while.

14:55.311 --> 14:57.522
Maybe I'll go lookin' for her.
Is that what you want?

15:02.318 --> 15:04.571
Look, I'm offerin' you
my services, Victor.

15:05.989 --> 15:07.574
You want me on your side, right?

15:10.660 --> 15:12.454
So, go tell your people
I want in,

15:12.454 --> 15:14.372
and let's get
this motherfuckin' money.

15:15.832 --> 15:16.708
We cool?

15:19.044 --> 15:21.046
Yo, welcome back to the hood,
baby!

15:22.005 --> 15:23.882
Let's get this money, Victor!

15:27.177 --> 15:28.762
[thudding]

15:29.387 --> 15:31.639
- [door slams open]
- [lock clatters to floor]

15:32.182 --> 15:33.391
[tense music playing]

15:38.730 --> 15:41.107
[jangling, thudding]

15:41.107 --> 15:42.400
[jangling, clattering]

15:49.574 --> 15:51.576
- [rustling, thud]
- [Salvatore] Damn it!

15:56.706 --> 15:58.416
We gotta find
someone he cares about.

15:58.917 --> 16:00.126
He doesn't.

16:00.126 --> 16:02.003
- It's his greatest asset.
- [clicks]

16:03.755 --> 16:04.923
[books thud]

16:09.135 --> 16:10.345
[remote clicks]

16:10.345 --> 16:14.474
- [fire whooshes]
- [romantic guitar music plays]

16:14.599 --> 16:15.684
[music stops]

16:15.684 --> 16:16.643
I know.

16:25.360 --> 16:26.945
Hey, hey, hey, hey.

16:27.612 --> 16:28.446
Who are they?

16:29.322 --> 16:30.323
His brothers.

16:31.116 --> 16:32.450
They died young.

16:32.992 --> 16:34.285
His mother is dead, too.

16:34.994 --> 16:36.996
I never heard much
about his father.

16:37.580 --> 16:38.665
So he's got nothing.

16:42.252 --> 16:44.212
He takes everything from me,

16:44.212 --> 16:45.797
and he's got nothing!

16:47.132 --> 16:48.466
Nothing! [pounds table]

16:51.344 --> 16:52.345
Practice your swing.

16:56.266 --> 16:57.434
- [grunts]
- [shattering]

16:57.434 --> 16:58.852
[thudding and shattering]

16:58.852 --> 17:00.729
[Salvatore grunting]

17:05.650 --> 17:06.526
[Salvatore] Shit.

17:07.110 --> 17:09.362
- [thudding and shattering]
- [Salvatore grunting]

17:12.449 --> 17:14.367
[thudding and shattering
continue]

17:36.890 --> 17:37.807
[grunts]

17:44.356 --> 17:45.357
[water running]

17:52.238 --> 17:53.198
Hey, Ma.

17:54.074 --> 17:54.949
[belches]

17:54.949 --> 17:56.159
Ma, you hungry?

17:59.913 --> 18:01.289
[Francis] Oswald!

18:03.375 --> 18:04.542
Oswald!

18:04.668 --> 18:06.461
- Ma, you all right?
- [Francis] Help!

18:09.130 --> 18:10.840
Don't look at me!
Don't look at me! Don't look!

18:10.840 --> 18:12.050
Jesus, Ma!

18:12.592 --> 18:14.678
Ah, don't look at me! [groans]

18:14.678 --> 18:15.845
Ma, what happened?

18:15.845 --> 18:17.639
- Just get me outta here.
- Come here.

18:18.348 --> 18:19.724
- [Francis whimpers]
- You all right?

18:19.724 --> 18:20.934
- [whimpers]
- Ma.

18:21.059 --> 18:22.477
Ma, the water's
fucking freezing.

18:22.477 --> 18:23.645
How long you been in here?

18:23.895 --> 18:25.897
- Come on. Come on. There you go.
- [whimpering]

18:26.022 --> 18:27.857
- Up, up, up, up.
- [grunting]

18:27.857 --> 18:28.942
There you go.

18:30.443 --> 18:31.444
All right.

18:32.278 --> 18:33.238
Jesus Christ!

18:33.363 --> 18:34.739
- [mutters]
- Wait, wait, wait, wait.

18:34.864 --> 18:36.574
- [muttering] Quick.
- Wait, wait, wait.

18:37.909 --> 18:39.661
- We been at it all night.
- [mutters]

18:39.661 --> 18:41.788
I shoulda checked on ya.

18:42.330 --> 18:43.206
I'm sorry.

18:44.416 --> 18:45.250
[Oz grunts]

18:46.251 --> 18:48.586
[grunts] All right.
Okay, this leg. One leg.

18:49.462 --> 18:51.423
There you go. There you go.

18:52.173 --> 18:55.260
[grunting]

18:55.385 --> 18:57.053
There you go.
All right, let's go.

18:57.053 --> 18:58.763
Slow, slow, slow, slow, slow.

19:00.557 --> 19:02.100
All right.
Come on. You got it.

19:03.560 --> 19:04.602
There you go.

19:05.145 --> 19:06.021
Come on.

19:07.647 --> 19:09.816
[Francis whimpers, grunts]

19:09.941 --> 19:12.569
- [Francis whimpers, cries]
- [Oz shushes]

19:12.569 --> 19:15.488
[Francis whimpers] Please...
I can't...

19:15.488 --> 19:17.907
- I can't do this.
- [shushes] You're all right.

19:17.907 --> 19:19.409
Oswald, I can't do this.

19:19.409 --> 19:21.369
- Mm-mmm. I can't do this.
- Ma, listen to me.

19:21.369 --> 19:23.246
You're gonna be all right.
We just gotta--

19:23.246 --> 19:25.665
We just gotta get you warmed up.
That's all.

19:27.667 --> 19:29.419
[sniffles] This thing I got,

19:29.419 --> 19:31.838
it's a goddamn dirty thief.

19:31.963 --> 19:33.214
Just keeps taking.

19:34.299 --> 19:35.800
I can't do numbers no more.

19:36.593 --> 19:38.470
I'm seeing things
that ain't real.

19:39.471 --> 19:40.472
The boys...

19:40.972 --> 19:42.182
Sometimes, I see 'em.

19:44.100 --> 19:46.811
They look at me
like, like I ain't theirs.

19:48.646 --> 19:50.190
It breaks my goddamn heart.

19:50.940 --> 19:51.900
I know, Ma.

19:52.650 --> 19:55.153
I ain't gonna live
like a goddamn vegetable.

19:55.278 --> 19:56.738
I just ain't gonna do it.

19:56.738 --> 19:58.031
[sniffs] You understand?

19:58.156 --> 19:59.157
Yeah.

20:00.450 --> 20:02.494
Uh, no. What do you mean?

20:04.329 --> 20:07.165
If my mind goes
before my body's ready,

20:07.832 --> 20:11.169
I need you to help me.
You gotta help me die.

20:12.545 --> 20:13.630
Help you die? [splutters]

20:13.630 --> 20:15.423
Jesus, Ma,
you ain't thinkin' straight.

20:15.423 --> 20:16.508
For now, I am.

20:17.092 --> 20:19.052
I won't be one
of those pathetic old broads,

20:19.177 --> 20:22.180
droolin', shittin' themselves,

20:22.722 --> 20:24.432
starin' out at nothin'

20:24.432 --> 20:26.685
with no-no clue what's going on,

20:26.810 --> 20:28.853
knowing just enough
to make it worse.

20:29.646 --> 20:32.190
If I lose my dignity,
what else I got, huh?

20:35.485 --> 20:37.362
- I can't do it.
- Sure, you can.

20:37.862 --> 20:38.905
Look at me, sweetheart.

20:39.989 --> 20:41.366
Oh, you'll be all right.

20:42.409 --> 20:43.535
I know you will.

20:45.370 --> 20:46.871
You're my brave boy.

20:51.626 --> 20:53.294
[quietly] But you ain't
a fuckin' dog.

20:54.754 --> 20:56.047
[inhales]

20:56.047 --> 20:57.465
You're my ma. I mean...

20:58.550 --> 21:00.135
You're asking me
to do something...

21:00.885 --> 21:02.095
- It ain't natural.
- No!

21:03.888 --> 21:05.890
No! Don't you pussy out
on me, Oswald.

21:06.016 --> 21:06.975
I swear to God.

21:07.684 --> 21:10.395
I have given you everything.
I have given you everything.

21:10.520 --> 21:11.604
Yeah, you have.

21:12.522 --> 21:14.399
Say you'll do it. And mean it.

21:15.066 --> 21:16.276
'Cause you love me.

21:17.110 --> 21:17.986
Say it.

21:20.447 --> 21:21.322
Say it.

21:24.784 --> 21:25.660
All right.

21:29.039 --> 21:29.873
I'll do it.

21:31.833 --> 21:33.251
[sniffs, voice breaks] Good.

21:33.376 --> 21:34.252
All right?

21:37.339 --> 21:38.548
Good. [sniffs]

21:38.548 --> 21:41.051
Come on, let's get you dressed.
Come on.

21:42.802 --> 21:44.095
On the count of three, okay?

21:44.679 --> 21:46.931
- One, two, three.
- Three.

21:47.724 --> 21:49.100
["Put the Blame on Mame"
playing]

21:49.100 --> 21:52.145
♪ When Mrs. O'Leary's cow ♪

21:52.270 --> 21:53.772
♪ Kicked the lantern ♪

21:54.689 --> 21:57.275
♪ In Chicago town ♪

21:58.735 --> 22:01.654
♪ They say
that started the fire ♪

22:02.197 --> 22:05.450
♪ That burned Chicago down ♪

22:08.036 --> 22:11.289
♪ That's the story
that went around ♪

22:12.499 --> 22:15.960
♪ But here's the real lowdown ♪

22:17.671 --> 22:21.508
♪ Put the blame on Mame, boys ♪

22:22.384 --> 22:25.178
♪ Put the blame on Mame ♪

22:26.179 --> 22:29.974
♪ Mame kissed a buyer
from out of town... ♪

22:30.100 --> 22:31.309
Oswald.

22:33.019 --> 22:34.479
You look gorgeous, Ma.

22:36.314 --> 22:37.190
Powerful.

22:39.150 --> 22:40.151
Like Gilda.

22:40.276 --> 22:42.904
♪ Put the blame on Mame ♪

22:43.488 --> 22:44.322
[song ends]

22:53.331 --> 22:54.207
[door closes]

22:58.003 --> 23:00.088
Hey.

23:03.133 --> 23:04.009
Uh...

23:04.843 --> 23:06.511
Rest of the drops went smooth.

23:07.512 --> 23:11.349
Bliss is all over the streets.
You, uh, h-hear anything yet?

23:11.850 --> 23:12.767
Nah.

23:15.186 --> 23:16.146
[click]

23:17.147 --> 23:18.023
[engine stalls]

23:18.982 --> 23:19.983
Um...

23:19.983 --> 23:21.735
- [engine stalls]
- There's something...

23:23.236 --> 23:26.072
We maybe got a... problem.

23:26.906 --> 23:27.782
Uh...

23:29.826 --> 23:34.039
There's this guy
f-f-from the neighborhood.

23:34.998 --> 23:36.374
Everybody calls him Squid.

23:37.500 --> 23:39.794
He's the guy
that I boosted your rims for.

23:39.794 --> 23:40.754
[Oz grunts]

23:43.048 --> 23:46.051
Well, look, I th-thought
I could avoid him, but...

23:47.510 --> 23:48.386
he's on me.

23:49.512 --> 23:53.892
A-asking questions about us,
and, uh...

23:56.394 --> 23:57.812
I don't think he's gonna stop.

23:57.812 --> 23:59.856
[engine stalls]

23:59.856 --> 24:01.399
This fuckin' thing.

24:08.615 --> 24:09.908
It's cold in here, right?

24:10.909 --> 24:13.453
[sighs] It's too fuckin' cold
for Ma.

24:16.456 --> 24:19.084
You know, they don't even know
what she's got.

24:22.212 --> 24:24.297
First, it was Parkinson's.
Then Alzheimer's.

24:24.422 --> 24:27.133
And now, they're talking
about some fuckin' thing

24:27.133 --> 24:29.469
called Lewy body.
What the fuck is that, huh?

24:31.638 --> 24:33.473
You know,
all these fuckin' geniuses,

24:33.598 --> 24:35.600
they got the diplomas
and machines.

24:35.725 --> 24:37.018
They don't even fuckin' know.

24:37.727 --> 24:40.438
How am I supposed to protect her
from something like that?

24:41.981 --> 24:44.776
[inhales] Y-you're doing
the best you can, though.

24:44.901 --> 24:46.361
She knows that.

24:46.361 --> 24:49.072
It's a good thing
that she's here with you.

24:49.197 --> 24:50.073
[Oz grunts]

24:50.699 --> 24:52.117
What you were saying before...

24:53.451 --> 24:54.285
[Victor] Hmm?

24:54.786 --> 24:55.662
We got a problem?

24:57.205 --> 24:58.415
No.

24:58.415 --> 24:59.874
No, no. I'm good.

25:00.500 --> 25:01.418
- You sure?
- Yep.

25:04.462 --> 25:05.463
[Oz] Look at that.

25:06.840 --> 25:08.800
City Hall shinin' bright.

25:11.803 --> 25:12.637
[clicking]

25:16.808 --> 25:17.809
Keep an eye out.

25:18.643 --> 25:19.519
All right?

25:20.020 --> 25:21.021
[Victor] Mm-hmm.

25:23.273 --> 25:24.691
[dance music playing faintly]

25:25.650 --> 25:26.985
[Sofia] Her name's Eve.

25:29.988 --> 25:32.866
- Sorry. Never seen her.
- No.

25:33.992 --> 25:34.993
You sure about that?

25:35.493 --> 25:37.078
Never seen the bitch.

25:41.541 --> 25:42.917
[sirens in distance]

25:44.377 --> 25:47.005
You're a real buzzkill
around here, you know?

25:50.800 --> 25:51.885
Roxy.

25:53.011 --> 25:54.512
We met at Apex.

25:55.138 --> 25:56.264
Doubt you remember.

25:57.974 --> 26:00.268
But I might be able to help.

26:01.478 --> 26:02.896
For the right price.

26:05.982 --> 26:07.192
[indistinct conversation]

26:09.027 --> 26:10.320
Appreciate your time,
Councilman.

26:10.320 --> 26:12.364
Anything for the GCPD.

26:12.489 --> 26:13.531
These days especially,

26:13.656 --> 26:15.325
we need to look out
for one another.

26:15.325 --> 26:18.203
[conversation continues
indistinctly]

26:19.329 --> 26:21.039
- [laughing]
- See you next week.

26:21.164 --> 26:22.290
Good night, guys.

26:24.834 --> 26:27.420
Come on! Who is this asshole?

26:27.962 --> 26:29.047
Clunker.

26:30.131 --> 26:31.132
[Oz] Councilman Hady.

26:34.135 --> 26:35.220
Carmine's guy.

26:35.720 --> 26:37.972
I wrote you a note, you know.
You never responded.

26:38.890 --> 26:40.558
You don't wanna be pals with me?

26:41.101 --> 26:43.645
Kinda, you know,
hurts my feelings.

26:44.354 --> 26:45.814
Listen, I paid off my debts.

26:45.814 --> 26:47.232
Yeah, yeah. To Carmine.

26:47.774 --> 26:48.733
Not to me.

26:49.776 --> 26:50.735
Okay.

26:51.736 --> 26:54.114
"Okay"? What,
you think I don't matter?

26:54.114 --> 26:55.990
That it?
Then you don't mind too much

26:55.990 --> 26:58.493
if I introduce myself
to some of your crooked friends?

26:58.493 --> 26:59.619
- Huh? Huh?
- Hey.

26:59.744 --> 27:00.787
Come here. Come here.

27:00.912 --> 27:02.997
- Come here.
- [grunts] Stop! Stop!

27:02.997 --> 27:05.083
Or maybe I just, uh,
talk to the Gazette?

27:05.208 --> 27:06.418
I bet they'd love to see

27:06.543 --> 27:08.420
how you paid your gambling debts
with city funds.

27:08.545 --> 27:09.838
[Hady grunts]

27:09.838 --> 27:11.631
You think you can just raw dog
the people of Gotham

27:11.756 --> 27:13.049
with an invisible dick? That it?

27:13.049 --> 27:15.760
Shit! [grunts]
Shit! What do you want?

27:15.885 --> 27:17.762
I want you to do
your fuckin' job.

27:17.887 --> 27:19.347
That's what I fuckin' want.

27:19.347 --> 27:20.598
[groaning]

27:20.724 --> 27:22.559
City's diverting power
from Crown Point.

27:22.559 --> 27:24.936
Families are living in the dark.
They're freezing.

27:25.478 --> 27:27.647
Meanwhile, you go home
to your warm fuckpad mansion.

27:27.772 --> 27:29.274
- It ain't right.
- [groaning]

27:29.816 --> 27:31.776
So you're gonna get
the power on in Crown Point.

27:31.901 --> 27:34.612
You know how much red tape and--
[screams in pain]

27:34.738 --> 27:36.364
Please stop!
I'll do it! I'll do it!

27:36.364 --> 27:38.283
Please stop! Fuck!
[cries out in pain]

27:38.408 --> 27:40.076
- Please stop! Fuck!
- All right. All right.

27:40.076 --> 27:42.787
- [moaning in pain]
- Hey, hey. It's just your nose.

27:42.912 --> 27:44.497
Fuckin' hell. Give me your tie.

27:45.749 --> 27:46.624
Listen to me.

27:47.250 --> 27:48.501
You got till sunup.

27:49.252 --> 27:51.296
And I ain't someone's guy.
My name's Oswald Cobb.

27:52.297 --> 27:53.798
Next time, you won't forget.

27:54.257 --> 27:55.842
- [whimpers]
- Get the fuck outta here.

27:57.469 --> 27:58.511
[engine starts]

28:02.640 --> 28:03.850
Jesus! Come on.

28:03.975 --> 28:05.268
You got more room
than you think.

28:05.268 --> 28:06.394
Straight back.

28:06.978 --> 28:09.189
[phone ringing]

28:11.149 --> 28:12.192
Christ.

28:13.985 --> 28:15.445
Donny Boy, glad you called.

28:15.445 --> 28:16.863
What the fuck
you think you're doing

28:16.988 --> 28:18.615
dumping your product
in my territory?

28:18.615 --> 28:20.408
The fuck you talking about?
We had a deal.

28:20.408 --> 28:22.118
You turned your back.
What do you expect?

28:22.118 --> 28:23.953
Fuck you!
They murdered my boys.

28:23.953 --> 28:25.205
Put them on display...

28:25.205 --> 28:26.498
I ain't talkin' to you when--

28:26.623 --> 28:28.375
I ain't talkin' to you
when you're like this.

28:29.000 --> 28:30.210
Let's get together. We'll...

28:30.210 --> 28:31.836
We'll figure it out
face-to-face.

28:32.545 --> 28:34.422
- I know somewhere.
- Don't fuck with the Sullivans.

28:34.422 --> 28:36.007
I'm gonna text you the address.

28:36.508 --> 28:37.842
[train passing]

28:43.515 --> 28:44.557
[Squid] Yo, Victor.

28:45.475 --> 28:47.394
Freezin' my fuckin' dick off
out here.

28:48.061 --> 28:49.145
Where your people at?

28:49.145 --> 28:50.188
Uh...

28:50.730 --> 28:53.817
Right. So that's actually, uh,

28:53.817 --> 28:56.236
what I wanted
to talk to you about. Um...

28:57.278 --> 28:59.656
Look, man, I tried.
Okay? They're just not...

28:59.656 --> 29:03.076
They're not looking
for... more guys right now.

29:03.201 --> 29:05.537
But... Look.

29:07.330 --> 29:09.541
I know this is
your neighborhood, right?

29:10.500 --> 29:13.962
They know that, respect that,
respect you, so...

29:16.715 --> 29:17.632
Yeah.

29:20.051 --> 29:21.886
And look, man,
I can get you more next week.

29:22.012 --> 29:23.555
And-and...

29:24.556 --> 29:26.224
as soon as something opens up,

29:26.975 --> 29:27.851
you know?

29:28.393 --> 29:29.394
We just gotta...

29:30.437 --> 29:32.230
pump the brakes
and-and-and take things slow.

29:32.355 --> 29:33.982
But you can get me more
next week?

29:35.275 --> 29:37.277
- Right, yeah.
- 'Cause I'm already running low.

29:37.944 --> 29:39.821
Shit's crazy. It's going fast.

29:41.197 --> 29:42.449
What, you think you big, Victor?

29:43.450 --> 29:45.785
Think you can pay me off? Huh?

29:45.785 --> 29:48.371
You just a kid from the Bricks
who can't even steal some rims

29:48.371 --> 29:49.956
thinkin' he's big-time tough guy

29:50.081 --> 29:52.334
'cause he's working
with Oz what's-his-fuck.

29:52.334 --> 29:55.086
Yeah, the Wizard of fuckin' Oz.
Nobody sees this guy,

29:55.211 --> 29:57.255
but he's out here
pullin' all these strings.

29:58.381 --> 29:59.382
The word on the street is

29:59.382 --> 30:00.759
he's running that new drug,
Bliss,

30:00.884 --> 30:02.844
and a bunch of heavy-hitters
are lookin' for him.

30:02.844 --> 30:05.597
Maybe I should help them out,
make some real money.

30:07.891 --> 30:09.351
Or you take me to your boss.

30:10.435 --> 30:12.145
So what's it gonna be, Victor?

30:13.605 --> 30:14.481
Squid,

30:15.315 --> 30:16.232
Oz...

30:17.108 --> 30:18.318
he'll kill you.

30:18.318 --> 30:20.820
Yeah? Take me
to that motherfucker right now.

30:20.820 --> 30:22.906
- You think I'm playing with you?
- All right. Okay.

30:22.906 --> 30:25.283
All right. Yeah. Okay.

30:31.456 --> 30:32.624
Yo, lead the way.

30:32.749 --> 30:33.792
Uh... [exhales]

30:34.959 --> 30:35.960
We're this way.

30:37.837 --> 30:40.590
See? You a man now, Victor.

30:40.590 --> 30:42.634
Don't gotta make it
so hard on yourself.

30:44.511 --> 30:45.512
Look, Squid, he's...

30:46.554 --> 30:49.265
he's not even gonna be-be back
for another few hours.

30:49.265 --> 30:52.018
That's good with me. I'll wait.

30:59.401 --> 31:01.861
Okay, we're underground.

31:01.861 --> 31:02.987
Underground?

31:03.113 --> 31:04.531
Shit, you diggin' holes
or something?

31:04.531 --> 31:07.492
- [gun fires]
- [Squid gasps, gurgles]

31:07.617 --> 31:09.411
[gasps] Oh!

31:10.203 --> 31:12.163
- Ugh.
- [Squid gagging]

31:15.375 --> 31:17.836
[coughs wetly]

31:17.961 --> 31:20.171
Oh. Fuck.

31:20.296 --> 31:23.842
- [Squid coughing blood]
- Ah! Ah! [gasps]

31:23.967 --> 31:25.593
Oh, my God.

31:26.219 --> 31:27.637
[gasping]

31:27.637 --> 31:29.848
[somber music playing]

31:31.975 --> 31:33.768
[breathing heavily]

31:33.768 --> 31:35.854
I'm sorry. I'm sorry. I'm sorry.

31:38.314 --> 31:39.733
Why'd you make me do that?

31:40.358 --> 31:41.693
You fuck!

31:41.693 --> 31:43.153
[music intensifies]

31:43.153 --> 31:44.779
[helicopter passing overhead]

31:53.872 --> 31:55.540
[indistinct chatter in distance]

31:59.210 --> 32:00.545
[knocks on door]

32:06.009 --> 32:06.885
Hey.

32:10.555 --> 32:12.557
What? Didn't recognize me?

32:21.941 --> 32:23.068
[door closes]

32:24.736 --> 32:26.654
You don't seem surprised
to see me.

32:26.654 --> 32:28.740
I told Roxy to send you up.

32:29.741 --> 32:31.076
Save us both a headache.

32:31.951 --> 32:33.161
Easy money, too.

32:36.039 --> 32:36.915
Drink?

32:44.381 --> 32:45.590
Where is he?

32:45.757 --> 32:48.426
He'd never tell someone like me
something like that.

32:49.552 --> 32:51.513
You know Oz as well as I do.

33:10.990 --> 33:12.117
Dressing like this...

33:13.451 --> 33:14.994
is this for you or your clients?

33:15.620 --> 33:18.373
Depends on the situation.

33:20.291 --> 33:22.293
Oz ever seen
this version of you?

33:23.253 --> 33:25.296
Couple of times.
He doesn't like it.

33:27.048 --> 33:28.466
What does he like?

33:31.886 --> 33:34.139
He's not that complicated.

33:34.639 --> 33:35.557
[Sofia] Hmm.

33:36.182 --> 33:37.142
So...

33:39.519 --> 33:40.478
he's...

33:41.479 --> 33:44.649
[breathily] ...the best
you've ever had.

33:46.484 --> 33:47.360
What else?

33:48.653 --> 33:49.654
He's...

33:50.655 --> 33:53.408
[breathily] ...destined
for greatness.

33:58.580 --> 34:00.373
I used to lie to men like that.

34:02.042 --> 34:04.002
But you don't have to anymore.

34:06.504 --> 34:08.214
You have the power now.

34:10.008 --> 34:12.677
You are good at telling people
what they wanna hear.

34:19.934 --> 34:21.061
[sighs]

34:22.270 --> 34:24.856
You have a drawer at his place.

34:26.900 --> 34:28.526
You mean something to him.

34:29.069 --> 34:31.529
He won't come for me,
if that's your plan.

34:32.739 --> 34:34.908
Not that kind of relationship.
Okay.

34:36.701 --> 34:37.660
What is it then?

34:40.872 --> 34:42.749
He pays you, I presume, so...

34:43.667 --> 34:44.542
can't be love.

34:45.418 --> 34:46.961
Must be nice.

34:46.961 --> 34:49.089
You were born into opportunity,
honey,

34:49.089 --> 34:52.592
so you can afford
to think in black and white.

34:54.094 --> 34:57.639
What I got with Oz,
it ain't just one thing.

34:58.431 --> 35:00.058
I know what he is...

35:02.602 --> 35:04.896
a liar, narcissist...

35:06.064 --> 35:07.065
killer.

35:11.027 --> 35:12.612
But we all got our shit,
don't we?

35:12.737 --> 35:14.280
I mean, you certainly got yours.

35:17.701 --> 35:19.452
Nancy Hoffman...

35:20.412 --> 35:22.580
Yolanda Jones...

35:23.081 --> 35:24.749
those women meant nothing
to you.

35:25.917 --> 35:27.293
They were family to me.

35:29.462 --> 35:30.755
You still think I'm the Hangman?

35:34.884 --> 35:36.177
He never told you?

35:40.223 --> 35:41.808
My father killed those women.

35:44.394 --> 35:45.603
Killed my mother.

35:46.688 --> 35:47.564
Oz knew.

35:48.815 --> 35:50.191
He has always known.

35:51.151 --> 35:53.194
Well, he helped cover it up

35:53.194 --> 35:55.488
so that my father
could keep on killing women.

35:57.741 --> 35:58.700
He used me.

36:00.285 --> 36:02.162
He let me rot in Arkham,

36:03.246 --> 36:04.289
so he could move up.

36:06.875 --> 36:08.126
[Eve sighs]

36:09.044 --> 36:11.004
Kept you in the dark
about all that, huh?

36:13.173 --> 36:14.883
Well, I guess if he hadn't,

36:14.883 --> 36:17.802
you'd have asked questions
about him.

36:17.927 --> 36:20.013
How he knows?

36:20.138 --> 36:24.976
Why he would work for a man
that murdered your friends?

36:25.643 --> 36:27.145
Oz would never risk that.

36:28.688 --> 36:30.023
It's better for him...

36:32.275 --> 36:34.652
isn't it, if you fear me?

36:35.195 --> 36:37.822
He said he felt bad for you,
that you were sick.

36:37.947 --> 36:40.408
If that were true, you would've
been dead at the door.

36:41.451 --> 36:43.745
But you did come here
to kill me, right?

36:44.704 --> 36:46.831
I mean, after all
is said and done?

36:51.628 --> 36:52.921
You were his alibi.

36:54.130 --> 36:55.215
You knew.

36:56.383 --> 36:57.842
Not at first.

36:59.010 --> 37:00.178
But yeah.

37:04.641 --> 37:05.517
[gun cocks]

37:07.852 --> 37:11.106
So, when you're done here,

37:12.232 --> 37:14.359
just leave my girls alone, okay?

37:14.818 --> 37:16.403
That's why you asked me here?

37:19.656 --> 37:20.907
To save them.

37:21.491 --> 37:22.701
From the Hangman.

37:23.910 --> 37:25.704
But that's not
who you are, right?

37:29.165 --> 37:30.583
[pensive music playing]

37:36.715 --> 37:38.425
Your people protected you.

37:40.135 --> 37:41.428
They wouldn't give you up.

37:42.846 --> 37:44.097
Cuts both ways.

37:46.933 --> 37:48.143
They got my back.

37:48.935 --> 37:50.228
I got theirs.

37:56.901 --> 37:58.653
[gun rattles]

38:02.365 --> 38:04.451
Well, whatever I was born into,

38:07.078 --> 38:08.413
I'll never have that.

38:19.466 --> 38:21.009
Crown Point.

38:24.262 --> 38:25.930
By the Zoo.

38:28.099 --> 38:28.933
[Eve sighs]

38:35.648 --> 38:37.150
You deserve your shot.

38:40.570 --> 38:42.781
But where you got
that information...

38:44.616 --> 38:45.950
It'll stay between us.

38:48.161 --> 38:49.954
[dramatic music playing]

38:52.290 --> 38:55.835
- [motorcycle approaching]
- [dramatic music continues]

39:03.468 --> 39:04.386
[engine turns off]

39:07.347 --> 39:09.140
- [thuds heavily]
- Careful, fellas.

39:10.058 --> 39:12.936
Don't want this spillin'.
It'll ruin the surprise.

39:12.936 --> 39:15.146
Nick, you're driving.
Bruno, I need you to hang back,

39:15.271 --> 39:16.731
make sure
everything runs smoothly here.

39:16.731 --> 39:18.316
Whatever happens tonight,
fellas,

39:19.317 --> 39:20.235
we gotta be ready.

39:21.277 --> 39:22.404
Vic, where you been?

39:22.404 --> 39:24.406
Phone's been blowing up nonstop.

39:25.365 --> 39:27.409
Motherfuckers are pissed,
but they wanna meet.

39:27.867 --> 39:28.785
This is it.

39:31.705 --> 39:32.664
You good?

39:38.503 --> 39:39.421
What's up with you?

39:42.048 --> 39:43.091
Something with that guy?

39:49.681 --> 39:51.057
You get away clean?

39:52.851 --> 39:55.061
[inhales sharply]
I think so, yeah.

39:56.438 --> 39:58.356
D-don't look down. Meet me here.

40:01.693 --> 40:03.194
You done the right thing.

40:04.362 --> 40:06.031
Protected those you care about.

40:08.867 --> 40:10.201
You're strong, kid.

40:11.995 --> 40:13.538
[Oz exhales]

40:15.331 --> 40:16.541
[Victor exhales shakily]

40:20.503 --> 40:21.713
[quietly] It gets easier.

40:29.179 --> 40:30.555
I want you home tonight.

40:33.350 --> 40:34.559
Dump those clothes.

40:36.019 --> 40:37.479
All right? Clean yourself up.

40:38.271 --> 40:40.690
Get something to eat and rest,
all right?

40:40.690 --> 40:42.984
Or you're gonna be
a puddle of water tomorrow.

40:42.984 --> 40:45.236
I'm gonna need you. You hear me?

40:46.404 --> 40:47.238
Yeah?

40:48.615 --> 40:49.574
All right.

40:50.367 --> 40:51.743
[ominous music playing]

40:58.124 --> 40:59.918
[intense dramatic music playing]

41:07.050 --> 41:08.760
[intense dramatic music
continues]

41:22.148 --> 41:23.149
[Oz] Well, well, well...

41:23.733 --> 41:25.193
Late to my own party.

41:25.193 --> 41:26.528
It's not a good look, I know.

41:27.070 --> 41:29.030
[scraping, thudding]

41:30.323 --> 41:32.158
I got a little surprise
for you here.

41:35.120 --> 41:38.123
What I'm bringing you tonight
is big, bigger than Bliss.

41:38.248 --> 41:42.043
It's gonna change the face
of the whole city forever.

41:44.087 --> 41:47.966
And... it's my gift
to all of ya.

41:51.094 --> 41:52.345
This a fuckin' joke?

41:52.345 --> 41:55.181
Relax, Able.
Have a fuckin' beer. Jesus.

41:56.099 --> 41:57.684
You vouched for this man?

41:57.809 --> 41:59.310
That's right, Zhao, he did.

42:00.311 --> 42:01.855
And you're gonna thank him
for it.

42:02.856 --> 42:05.900
Ladies and gentlemen,
welcome to the Gold Summit.

42:06.609 --> 42:08.403
You'll be proud
to say you were here tonight,

42:08.403 --> 42:09.362
all of you...

42:10.113 --> 42:12.407
even though I know you hate
each other's friggin' guts.

42:12.407 --> 42:15.702
The shit between the Massive
and Odessa is legendary.

42:15.827 --> 42:17.787
LoBoys, you gotta scrap
with everyone

42:17.787 --> 42:19.205
just to get a bit of respect.

42:19.205 --> 42:23.251
Got the Triads.
Sullivans, oldest crew in town.

42:23.251 --> 42:25.837
But the most hated
here among us...

42:27.464 --> 42:29.466
is yours truly,
and not for nothin'.

42:29.466 --> 42:32.344
I got three of my guys strung up
'cause of you.

42:32.469 --> 42:34.721
No, not 'cause of me.

42:35.388 --> 42:37.140
They're dead
because the Maronis and Gigantes

42:37.140 --> 42:38.516
got the power to take you out.

42:38.683 --> 42:41.102
You want revenge?
What the fuck is stoppin' ya?

42:41.102 --> 42:42.562
They're right over there...

42:43.646 --> 42:45.315
across the Elliot Bridge.

42:45.982 --> 42:48.818
A bridge that was built
by your ancestors, Donny Boy,

42:48.818 --> 42:50.862
but it ain't named Sullivan.
Huh?

42:50.987 --> 42:52.781
No, it's named
for the rich crooks

42:52.781 --> 42:55.033
who took credit
for your family's hard work.

42:56.034 --> 42:58.286
They run shit. We eat shit.

42:58.286 --> 43:00.246
The sad thing, Donny Boy, is

43:00.997 --> 43:03.416
they don't even know
your fuckin' name!

43:06.711 --> 43:08.171
They don't know none of youse.

43:08.171 --> 43:09.214
But I do.

43:09.714 --> 43:11.257
Sal... Give me a fuckin' break.

43:11.257 --> 43:13.885
You know Sal bitches and moans

43:13.885 --> 43:16.388
about Carmine stealin'
his Drops business?

43:17.180 --> 43:20.058
What do you think him and Sofia
are gonna do to you, huh?

43:20.600 --> 43:23.311
They'll take your shit,
your territories.

43:23.311 --> 43:24.729
That's what's comin'.

43:25.689 --> 43:26.898
'Cause you mean nothin' to 'em.

43:27.691 --> 43:29.442
They don't give a fuck
about any of you all.

43:30.276 --> 43:31.945
You know,
not even a mile from here,

43:32.612 --> 43:35.281
there's a bunch of big-time,
City Hall fucks.

43:35.281 --> 43:37.200
They're sittin'
in some fancy private club.

43:37.200 --> 43:38.493
They're drinkin' orange wine.

43:38.493 --> 43:40.995
They're makin' crooked deals
to benefit them.

43:42.038 --> 43:44.499
And guess what? They can't
fuckin' stand each other either,

43:44.499 --> 43:45.750
just like you.

43:46.251 --> 43:47.877
But they're breakin' bread
because they know

43:47.877 --> 43:50.296
that each of them on their own,
they ain't got nothin',

43:50.296 --> 43:52.340
but together,
those soft-bellied pricks,

43:52.340 --> 43:54.175
they run
this whole fuckin' city.

43:55.051 --> 43:56.678
Why the hell not us?

43:58.263 --> 43:59.931
Now, I'm bringing you Bliss.

44:00.056 --> 44:02.142
Yeah, sure,
that gives us the extra leg.

44:02.892 --> 44:06.354
But the real power comes
if we've got each other's backs.

44:07.439 --> 44:09.899
Then Sal, Sofia, the old guard,

44:09.899 --> 44:11.693
they won't be able
to fuckin' touch us.

44:11.693 --> 44:13.153
[Zhao] This man's a fool.

44:13.153 --> 44:15.447
He betrays everyone
he works with.

44:15.947 --> 44:17.323
Sofia Gigante,

44:18.491 --> 44:19.826
Alberto Falcone.

44:20.827 --> 44:22.912
There's no code, no class.

44:22.912 --> 44:25.290
The Penguin is
a bargain-basement hustler.

44:25.415 --> 44:26.499
[foreboding music playing]

44:26.624 --> 44:28.585
He'll do anything, say anything,

44:28.585 --> 44:30.337
and everyone here knows it.

44:30.462 --> 44:31.963
[Oz] Do they, Zhao?

44:33.506 --> 44:35.050
'Cause here's what I know.

44:35.050 --> 44:38.136
Between us, we got
more territory, more manpower

44:38.261 --> 44:39.679
than this city's ever seen.

44:40.347 --> 44:42.390
You wanna blow that away?
Shit, go ahead.

44:42.390 --> 44:44.726
But I do got a fuckin' code!

44:47.103 --> 44:49.564
And I'm puttin' my goddamn life
on the line to share it with ya.

44:49.564 --> 44:52.150
If we come together
right here, right now,

44:53.443 --> 44:55.487
they're gonna talk
about this night...

44:57.280 --> 44:58.448
the time that we decided

44:58.448 --> 45:00.909
that it's better to work
with the ones we hate

45:00.909 --> 45:01.993
than live under those

45:02.202 --> 45:04.662
that don't even know
our fuckin' names!

45:06.289 --> 45:07.916
[tense music playing]

45:14.339 --> 45:15.423
Nick, give me a beer.

45:26.017 --> 45:27.769
Look, everything you heard
about me...

45:28.687 --> 45:30.063
is true, you know?

45:30.605 --> 45:32.524
I stole Sofia's product. I...

45:34.025 --> 45:35.694
I popped Alberto Falcone.

45:37.362 --> 45:38.238
I did it all.

45:39.656 --> 45:40.824
So fuckin' what?

45:44.035 --> 45:45.245
I hustle.

45:45.370 --> 45:46.246
You know, I...

45:48.248 --> 45:49.416
do what it takes.

45:51.668 --> 45:54.295
'Cause at the end of the day,
you know...

45:55.672 --> 45:56.798
[sighs]

45:57.841 --> 46:00.385
I'm just a poor kid
from the Eastside

46:00.510 --> 46:02.053
who's got something
to fuckin' prove.

46:03.596 --> 46:04.556
Like all of ya.

46:06.349 --> 46:07.392
[beer can opens]

46:12.564 --> 46:13.440
[beer can opens]

46:14.899 --> 46:20.071
[beer cans opening]

46:21.865 --> 46:24.784
[beer cans opening]

46:41.676 --> 46:42.510
[beer can opens]

46:43.094 --> 46:44.137
[beer can opens]

46:44.137 --> 46:45.889
[music intensifies]

47:00.070 --> 47:01.446
To taking back Gotham!

47:05.658 --> 47:06.659
[music ends]

47:09.829 --> 47:11.539
[sirens and traffic in distance]

47:17.253 --> 47:18.505
[breathing raggedly]

47:27.430 --> 47:29.849
- [electricity surges on]
- ["The Glow-Worm" plays loudly]

47:29.849 --> 47:33.728
[Francis exclaims]
Oswald! Oswald!

47:34.312 --> 47:36.648
[exclaims] What's happening?
What's going on?

47:36.773 --> 47:38.900
Hey, Francis,
the... power's back on.

47:38.900 --> 47:40.443
- Hold on.
- What time is it?

47:40.443 --> 47:43.571
- How do I--
- No, no, no, no. Leave it on.

47:43.571 --> 47:45.198
♪ Shine, little glow-worm... ♪

47:45.323 --> 47:46.658
[Francis] I love this song.

47:46.658 --> 47:49.953
♪ Hey, there
don't get dimmer, dimmer ♪

47:49.953 --> 47:52.789
♪ Light the path below, above ♪

47:52.789 --> 47:55.667
♪ And lead us on to love ♪

47:56.376 --> 47:58.628
[clapping to beat of music]
Whoa.

48:00.463 --> 48:01.339
Whoa.

48:03.967 --> 48:05.677
[humming along with song]

48:06.469 --> 48:07.846
[Francis laughs]

48:07.846 --> 48:10.056
- Dance with me, Benny.
- [thudding]

48:11.808 --> 48:12.934
You remember.

48:13.518 --> 48:15.353
Don't be shy, sweetheart.
Come here.

48:19.774 --> 48:20.859
You're my biscuit.

48:22.152 --> 48:23.403
Yeah. Yeah.

48:27.323 --> 48:28.658
[Francis laughs]

48:28.658 --> 48:31.494
♪ Glow little glow-worm,
fly of fire... ♪

48:31.494 --> 48:33.413
[laughing]

48:34.497 --> 48:38.126
One, two. One, two. One, two.
One, two. One, two.

48:38.126 --> 48:39.878
One, two. One, two.

48:40.587 --> 48:42.505
[snapping along with music]

48:42.505 --> 48:45.967
- [Victor chuckles]
- [Francis vocalizing]

48:49.387 --> 48:50.889
[Francis laughs]

48:51.014 --> 48:53.850
♪ Glow little glow-worm, glow ♪

48:53.850 --> 48:54.851
He did it.

48:55.935 --> 48:58.897
Oz got the power back on.

48:59.773 --> 49:01.066
Oswald did this?

49:02.108 --> 49:03.234
For you.

49:04.194 --> 49:06.279
He did it for you.

49:06.780 --> 49:09.908
♪ See how the shadows
deepen, darken ♪

49:10.033 --> 49:13.078
♪ You and your chick
should get to sparkin' ♪

49:13.078 --> 49:16.247
♪ I got a gal that I love so ♪

49:16.247 --> 49:18.208
♪ Glow little glow-worm, glow ♪

49:18.208 --> 49:19.292
[Francis] Oswald.

49:20.543 --> 49:23.922
- My boy! You did it!
- [music fades]

49:24.589 --> 49:25.757
My boy!

49:26.466 --> 49:27.425
Oswald!

49:27.550 --> 49:28.843
[Francis laughs]

49:28.843 --> 49:32.430
- [dramatic music playing]
- [song fades]

49:38.228 --> 49:40.188
["Black Flowers" by Chris Isaak
playing]

49:47.821 --> 49:50.990
♪ Children lying
in their beds ♪

49:51.950 --> 49:55.995
♪ Just remember
what your mother said ♪

49:55.995 --> 49:59.374
♪ Don't you worry
Don't you cry ♪

50:00.208 --> 50:05.213
♪ Little black flowers grow
in the sky ♪

50:07.257 --> 50:09.968
♪ In the sky ♪

50:12.137 --> 50:17.142
♪ I believed you ♪

50:17.267 --> 50:19.352
♪ I believed you ♪

50:20.395 --> 50:25.275
♪ I believed you ♪

50:25.400 --> 50:29.237
♪ When you said
you would be mine ♪

50:36.745 --> 50:41.833
♪ I believed you ♪

50:41.958 --> 50:45.003
♪ When you said you cried ♪

50:45.003 --> 50:49.090
♪ Believed you
when you said you'd try ♪

50:49.090 --> 50:54.346
♪ Believed you when you said
you loved me too ♪

50:56.890 --> 50:58.767
♪ I believed you ♪

51:01.061 --> 51:02.854
♪ I believed you ♪

51:05.732 --> 51:09.069
♪ I believed you ♪

